     The ssiiggppeennddiinngg() system call returns a mask of the signals pending for
     delivery to the calling thread or the calling process in the location in‐
     dicated by _s_e_t.  Signals may be pending because they are currently
     masked, or transiently before delivery (although the latter case is not
     normally detectable).

